{
  "explanation": "An attacker compromised the Jenkins service account and successfully leveraged 'sudo' privileges to establish persistence on the system. They first installed a malicious root crontab using a temporary file and subsequently enabled a persistent systemd service named 'dbus-update.service'. This indicates complete root-level compromise and ongoing unauthorized access.",
  "mitre_tactic": "Persistence",
  "recommended_actions": [
    "Immediately isolate the affected host (app-02) from the network to prevent further lateral movement or data exfiltration.",
    "Revoke and rotate all credentials, API keys, and secrets associated with the Jenkins service user and root access.",
    "Perform a comprehensive forensic investigation of the /tmp directory and analyze the contents of '/tmp/.k' and 'dbus-update.service' to fully scope the compromise."
  ]
}
